  "formal_acceptance_requirements": [
    "Treat watchdog status and exit code as cleanup evidence only: timed-out, malformed-slot and failed-coordinator cases can exit 0 after their trees terminate.",
    "A formal successful window additionally requires reason owner_exited, coordinator exit code 0, closing_input_guard_passed true, matching frozen source/protocol/input hashes, complete expected slot inventory, and independent numerical and isolation certification.",
    "Poll-based latest-slot observation may miss an intermediate terminal state. It does not by itself prove every slot ended before the next began; verify immutable per-slot terminal/identity records in the coordinator audit.",
    "Every pending record forbids automatic continuation. Later separately observed cleanup may be recorded as additional evidence without rewriting the original pending outcome.",
    "The CPU8 coordinator, CPU6 monitor, CPU4 worker integration is outside this review and needs its separate frozen-source review; this audit verifies watchdog observer CPU10 and owner CPU12 records only."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No claim of hard real-time return under arbitrary OS/driver failure: file reads, hash computation, flush/rename, process creation and other native calls remain synchronous.",
    "CPU fixtures establish tested behavior; they do not demonstrate GPU cleanup, driver health, or a cause of the earlier two-hour mid-window coordinator stagnation.",
    "Official JOB_LIST documentation supports creation-time assignment but this review does not generalize the fixtures into a proof of all possible creation interruption/rollback behavior.",
    "The input guard checks the supplied map; the eventual frozen formal request must bind all required inputs, including the executed helper binary and protocol.",
    "No formal ranking, performance result, release approval or permission to continue after pending is granted by this review."
  ],
